      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T16:38:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`fData` is meant to be able to house different kinds of data. Right now, it is only used for immutable sampler information. There is an outstanding bug (https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.h#91 ; b/347072931) to enable us to tie the data to snippet IDs which is what would allow us to know what type of data to expect and validate against.\n\nAdded more comment documentation which hopefully helps clarify this. Thanks for your perspective; having a fresh set of eyes always offers good insight.",
