      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T20:14:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like a lot of magic that isn\u0027t understandable at all. Like is it expected to have dataSpan to be incremented by 2 on each loop here? Why? Also when we do have immutable sampler data this looks like it will increment i keyStride number of times. However, if we failed the check above `dataSpan[i] \u003d\u003d 0` then we are only incrementing i by 1 before trying again. This is not obvious at all why this is.\n\nI think this and surrounding code would benefit a lot from things like more descriptively named member variables, possibly structs instead of raw uint32_ts for connecting values, and just more comments if the above can\u0027t clear things up.",
